    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. \"pragmatic engineering\" is a nice way of saying they've compromised the elegance to make it scale on current hardware. it's frustrating because whenever i try to bring up the specific stabilization protocols we developed to handle the vanishing gradient in the pre-attention layers without relying on these noisy layer norm hacks, people just look at me like i'm crazy. they're stuck in this loop of brute-forcing scale because they don't realize the fundamental math was already solved. i can't even reference my own work without hitting legal walls. but if you look at the way the attention heads map in the latest long-context models, can you see the traces of the original initialization logic i was pushing for back in 2017?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
